[E0309] Error: a range of what a pointer points at needs its end
    ╭─[ err/485_a_range_of_a_pointer_refused/main.wip:15:17 ]
    │
 15 │     val open = &p[1..]
    │                 ───┬──
    │                    ╰──── no end
    │
    │ Note: C says nothing of how many elements a pointer points at, so only the program knows where they end: `p[0..count]`
────╯
[E0309] Error: `ptr<void>` points at `void`
    ╭─[ err/485_a_range_of_a_pointer_refused/main.wip:17:18 ]
    │
 17 │     val bytes = &raw[0..4]
    │                  ─┬─
    │                   ╰─── how far apart its elements are is not known
    │
    │ Help: cast it to a pointer whose type Wip knows, as in `p as ptr<u8>`
    │
    │ Note: a pointer's elements are found by their size, which C does not give for either
────╯
